course: dictionary
lesson: 1905
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «colouring» can mean different things. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Zoos add pink colouring to flamingos' food» is about a substance you add to food, not about the birds' feathers or a picture.
explain: Ask yourself what the word is doing in the sentence. Is it a thing, an activity, or an action happening now? In «I am colouring the sky blue», colouring is something happening now, so it is a form of the verb colour.
explain: The same word can be a thing, like «a colouring book», or an activity, like colouring in a picture. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: «Colouring» can be a noun (a thing or an activity) or a form of the verb colour, meaning giving colour to something now.
fact: «Food colouring» is a substance added to food or drink to give it colour.
fact: «Colouring in» means filling in a picture with crayons, pencils or pens.
fact: «Camouflage is colouring that helps an animal blend in with its surroundings.»
fact: In American English the word is spelled «coloring», with no u.
exercise: «Zoos add pink colouring to flamingos' food.» What is the pink colouring? | A song the flamingos sing at dusk | A bright pink bowl for the birds to eat from | The pink feathers on the flamingos' wings | *A substance added to food to give it colour
exercise: Ella has a «colouring book» on her bed. What is a colouring book for? | Mixing paint for a big painting | Reading stories about the colours of the rainbow | *Filling in pictures with crayons or pencils | Learning how to swim
exercise: «Camouflage is colouring that helps an animal blend in with its surroundings.» What does camouflage colouring help an animal do? | Shine brightly in the sun | Warn others to stay away | *Blend in with the things around it | Run very fast
test: «I am colouring the sky blue.» In this sentence, what is happening? | The sky has been blue for years | *Someone is giving the sky colour right now | Someone is drawing a cloud | The sky is grey and wet
test: «Lucy's natural colouring is dark brown hair and brown eyes.» What does natural colouring mean here? | *The colour a person has naturally, such as hair and eyes | A picture Lucy drew in class | Paint that Lucy put on her hair | A colouring book Lucy likes
exam: Which sentence uses «colouring» to mean a substance added to food? | «She is colouring the cat grey.» | *«Mum bought red food colouring for the cake.» | «I like the colouring of the sunset.» | «We finished our colouring in the park.»
